    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3bd0b05e-a82a-5641-a301-e6a77af1abf1",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9u+7v &=-5 \\\\ 8u+4v &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order $u,v$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
