      "title": "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a Linear System With Variables Other Than x, y, z"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d09dea0e-b25e-54ff-8fe2-462b8bbcb4fd",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}8 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "aa3ffa57-4feb-5110-ae02-37a659655bc2",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
